│ before stopping                                                              │
│ - **ONLY** stop containers that were explicitly created by this session      │
│ - **ONLY** stop containers using their explicit name: `docker stop <exact-co │
│ ntainer-name>`                                                               │
│                                                                              │
│ **Process Management:**                                                      │
│ - **NEVER** run `killall`, `pkill`, or similar commands without specific pro │
│ cess names                                                                   │
│ - **NEVER** use `kill -9` on system processes or processes you didn't start  │
│ - **ONLY** terminate processes you explicitly started in this session        │
│                                                                              │
│ **Port/Network Conflicts:**                                                  │
│ - If a port is in use, **USE A DIFFERENT PORT** instead of killing the proce │
│ ss using it                                                                  │
│ - Check what's running on a port with `lsof -i :<port>` or `ss -tlnp | grep  │
│ <port>`                                                                      │
│ - Prefer random/high ports (e.g., `docker run -p 0:8080`) to avoid conflicts │
│                                                                              │
│ **General Safety:**                                                          │
│ - **NEVER** run commands that affect system-wide state unless explicitly req │
│ uired by the PRD                                                             │
│ - **NEVER** use wildcards or glob patterns with destructive commands (`rm`,  │
│ `kill`, `stop`)                                                              │
│ - When in doubt, be explicit and specific with resource names                │
